xl-calculator (0.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * On a Wayland desktop, xl-Calculator runs through XWayland (X11), so the
    Buffet menu opens just under its button and stays on screen. Setting
    GDK_BACKEND still chooses the backend.
  * The small icons (16, 24, and 32 pixels) are installed as PNG, with
    their drawings kept in data/icons.
  * Searching Add or Remove Currencies also matches each currency's
    English name, so "peso" finds the pesos in every language.
  * A Flatpak manifest, for Flathub, and a checklist for trying it on other
    desktops. Every link points at the repository's new address,
    github.com/xlcheese/xlcalculator.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xl-calculator (0.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Buffet menu: every menu at once, from a button in the title bar
    (F10, or Alt and a menu's underlined letter). Preferences has a Menu
    tab to change how it lays out its menus, or to go back to a menu bar.
    The menu titles now have access keys in the menu bar too.
  * The Currency Converter has 152 currencies: the United Nations
    Treasury's operational rates (fetched at most every two weeks) and the
    Bank of Canada's rate for the New Taiwan Dollar join the European
    Central Bank's. The menus offer the most traded currencies and the
    person's own; Add or Remove Currencies… (also in Preferences) chooses
    from all of them. The line under the boxes names each rate's source
    and date, and every currency has its own decimal places.
  * The shaded keys keep the theme's own highlights and drop shadows, and
    a key that changes style no longer makes the window grow.
  * A draft Russian translation, waiting for a review by a native speaker.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xl-calculator (0.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Xcalculator is now called xl-Calculator, alongside xl-Screenshot and
    xl-Annotate: the command and package are xl-calculator, and the app ID
    is io.github.xlcheese.XlCalculator. This package replaces xcalculator.
  * The first time it starts, xl-Calculator copies the settings, history,
    and downloaded rates kept under the old name, and moves the daily rates
    check over if it was switched on.
  * The title bar shows just the mode, such as "Basic".
  * The keypad's larger buttons no longer enlarge the title bar's buttons
    (when the title bar is a GTK header bar) or the Preferences window.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xcalculator (0.9.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A calmer keypad: the number keys and decimal point are left white and
    every other key takes a shade of the theme's text color, so the
    numbers stand out in any theme, light or dark.
  * Clear and backspace are no longer red, and Clear is bold. Backspace is
    also an icon at the right end of the display, in every mode.
  * Basic has a square root key (Ctrl+R) that works like a pocket
    calculator's: 9 √ gives 3.
  * The icon has a darker border, with a sharp edge at 16, 24, and 32 px.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

xcalculator (0.9.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Draft translations into Spanish, French, German, and Brazilian
    Portuguese, waiting for a review by native speakers.
  * Currency names are the official ISO 4217 names from iso-codes, in the
    desktop's language (iso-codes is now a dependency).
  * A new icon.
  * The history sits in a bordered box like the input field, with a
    scrollbar that only shows while scrolling, and takes its colors from
    the system theme. Status and error messages use the theme's text color.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xcalculator (0.9.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New Currency Converter mode (Ctrl+Alt+C), with the European Central
    Bank's exchange rates for about 30 currencies. Nothing is downloaded
    until Download Rates is clicked; the rates are kept for offline use.
  * Auto Refresh refreshes the rates every 1 to 30 days (3 to start),
    while Xcalculator is open, or also when it's closed if switched on in
    Preferences (a systemd user timer that only Xcalculator enables).
  * Preferences and Documentation wording reviewed: US English, serial
    commas, and a hint for every setting ending with a period.
  * Documentation pages wrap list items under their own text.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xcalculator (0.9.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Opening Xcalculator again, or File → New Window, opens another window in
    the same program. The windows share the Preferences settings and the
    saved history.
  * Settings and history are now kept in ~/.config/xcalculator/.
  * Every word on screen can be translated (gettext); translators start from
    po/xcalculator.pot.
  * The program is split into modules, one per mode.
  * Built with a small Makefile; the menu entry is now
    io.github.xlcheese.Xcalculator.desktop.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

